1. e4 c6 2. Nf3 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. d4 { Bishop on c8 often doesn't have a good home. Aim to develop the bishop quickly. } 4... Nc6 5. c3 { Drawback of Bg6 right now is Qb3 } { [%csl Bb7][%cal Rg8f6,Rc8g4,Bd1b3,Bb3b7] } 5... Nf6 6. Bb5 { Not common. But not afraid of the pin very much. Bg4 prevents ne5 } { [%csl Rc8] } 6... Bg4 7. Qd3 Bxf3 { Trade the bishop and eliminate the piece that could get trapped behind the pawns. } 8. Qxf3 e6 9. O-O { [%cal Gf8d6,Rc1g5,Bf8e7,Gh7h6] } 9... h6 (9... Bd6 { Slightly inaccurate as it allows Bg5. }) 10. Nd2 Bd6 11. Nb3 { [%csl Rc5][%cal Rc1f4,Rb3c5,Bd8c7] } 11... Qc7 { Prevents the bishop from developing out to f4, allowing a trade of the bishops and then White's knight arriving on c5. However, the knight is now a bit loose. } 12. g3 O-O 13. Bxh6 gxh6 14. Qxf6 *


